<Project>
    <PropertyGroup>
        <!-- NuGet Package Info -->
        <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
        <PackageId>$(MSBuildProjectName)</PackageId>
        <Version>1.2.0</Version>
        <Authors>Andrea Ficarra</Authors>
        <Copyright>Copyright © 2026 Andrea Ficarra</Copyright>
        <Description>Lightweight, free, open-source in-process mediator for .NET. Supports requests, streaming requests, notifications, pipeline behaviors, pre/post-processors, and pluggable notification sinks.</Description>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Adiakys/OpenMediator</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Adiakys/OpenMediator</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>
1.2.0:
- Add IRequestPreProcessor&lt;TRequest&gt; and IRequestPostProcessor&lt;TRequest, TResponse&gt; (MediatR-compatible). Multiple processors per request type are supported and execute in registration order; post-processors are skipped when the handler or any preceding step throws.
- Add explicit registration via cfg.AddRequestPreProcessor&lt;T&gt;() and cfg.AddRequestPostProcessor&lt;T&gt;(); the wrapper pipeline behaviors are wired automatically when at least one processor is registered.
- Add cfg.AutoRegisterRequestProcessors flag (default false) for opt-in assembly scanning of processors, mirroring MediatR.
- AddOpenMediatR no longer throws when no assemblies are configured to scan (matches MediatR); it registers core services and lets you compose the rest explicitly.
- Fix: AddOpenMediatR is now idempotent across multiple calls for scanned INotificationHandler&lt;&gt;, user pipeline behaviors registered via AddOpenBehavior/AddOpenStreamBehavior, and pre/post-processors (switched to TryAddEnumerable, deduplicating by service+implementation pair).
        </PackageReleaseNotes>
        <PackageTags>mediator;cqrs;pipeline;notifications;request-response;streaming;messaging;dotnet;open-source</PackageTags>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
        
        <!-- Build and Publish Settings -->
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
        <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- Optional: Additional files for the NuGet package -->
        <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
        <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
        <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)\..\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
